WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.967 --> 00:00:02.335
-Welcome back to "Late Night."

00:00:02.335 --> 00:00:03.503
We're here with Nick Kroll.
We discussed your parents.

00:00:03.503 --> 00:00:04.537
How, especially --

00:00:04.537 --> 00:00:06.172
You talk about childbirth
in this special.

00:00:06.172 --> 00:00:08.074
How does your wife respond
to the idea of putting

00:00:08.074 --> 00:00:09.442
her stories in your act?

00:00:09.442 --> 00:00:13.313
-Well, I think, my wife, Lily,
has been really helpful

00:00:13.313 --> 00:00:16.015
throughout the process of coming
up with working on this hour.

00:00:16.015 --> 00:00:17.884
And she was like,
"If you're gonna talk about,

00:00:17.884 --> 00:00:20.519
like, the birth of our child,
don't do some

00:00:20.519 --> 00:00:22.388
bull [bleep]
little joke about it," you know?

00:00:22.388 --> 00:00:27.426
And so, it forced me to kind of
actually get into what matters.

00:00:27.426 --> 00:00:30.162
And it helped me eventually
get to the point where,

00:00:30.162 --> 00:00:33.966
I make fun of moms, but then
in talking about childbirth,

00:00:33.966 --> 00:00:36.903
it's like you understand
why moms are so --

00:00:36.903 --> 00:00:40.005
we're so tied to our moms and
that complicated relationship.

00:00:40.005 --> 00:00:41.907
And I definitely would not
have gotten there without,

00:00:41.907 --> 00:00:45.078
like, really talking through
all that with my wife, Lily.

00:00:45.078 --> 00:00:46.879
So I'm very grateful to her.
-It's very special to have

00:00:46.879 --> 00:00:49.549
someone who can
collaborate that way on

00:00:49.549 --> 00:00:51.150
the writing of material
about important things.

00:00:51.150 --> 00:00:52.752
-Yes.
I mean, she writes all my jokes.

00:00:52.752 --> 00:00:54.420
I am a vessel for them.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:54.420 --> 00:00:55.889
-Yeah, absolutely.

00:00:55.889 --> 00:00:57.857
And then my --
Alexi writes all my jokes

00:00:57.857 --> 00:00:59.325
and is very hard on me
when I get it wrong.

00:00:59.325 --> 00:01:00.293
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:00.293 --> 00:01:02.361
She's backstage, like -- yeah.

00:01:02.361 --> 00:01:03.530
-"Stick to what was
on the page."

00:01:03.530 --> 00:01:06.065
-Yeah, like a dance mom.
She's like, "You failed!"

00:01:06.065 --> 00:01:07.500
[ Laughter ]

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:10.136
You took --
you did something very risky.

00:01:10.136 --> 00:01:12.238
-Mm-hmm.
-You had a movie premiere

00:01:12.238 --> 00:01:13.640
at the Venice Film Festival.
-Yes.

00:01:13.640 --> 00:01:16.576
-And you went on a red-eye
with a 1 1/2-year-old.

00:01:16.576 --> 00:01:20.546
-Yes, me and my wife,
and we flew with our son.

00:01:20.546 --> 00:01:22.948
You know, when you fly,
your worst nightmare is,

00:01:22.948 --> 00:01:25.918
you fly with your child and that
your child is gonna be loud

00:01:25.918 --> 00:01:27.653
and unpleasant on a plane.
-Yeah.

00:01:27.653 --> 00:01:29.155
-And we thought
we had timed it well.

00:01:29.155 --> 00:01:31.123
Like, we got --
It was a 7:00 flight.

00:01:31.123 --> 00:01:33.726
We get on there with him.
You know, we've got all his --

00:01:33.726 --> 00:01:35.428
We put him in his
little sleep sack, you know.

00:01:35.428 --> 00:01:36.762
For those of you
who don't have kids,

00:01:36.762 --> 00:01:40.066
sleep sacks are like
a sleeping bag with a tank top.

00:01:40.066 --> 00:01:42.402
And I'm like,
"Oh, I want to wear that.

00:01:42.402 --> 00:01:45.572
Why don't they make
an adult-sized that?"

00:01:45.572 --> 00:01:48.241
And then, you know,
we get him ready for bed.

00:01:48.241 --> 00:01:49.475
We start reading him some books.

00:01:49.475 --> 00:01:51.176
We read him all of
the light-night show hosts.

00:01:51.176 --> 00:01:54.814
We read him Kimmel's book,
we read him Fallon's book,

00:01:54.814 --> 00:01:57.884
uh, Corden's book...
[ Laughter ]

00:01:57.884 --> 00:02:00.620
...and, um...
-And --

00:02:00.620 --> 00:02:02.288
Greg Gutfeld's book.
-Oh, my God.

00:02:02.288 --> 00:02:04.023
And, um...
[ Laughter ]

00:02:04.023 --> 00:02:06.493
"Here's What the Libs Don't
Want You to Know About Sleep."

00:02:06.493 --> 00:02:08.294
-It is very good.
I don't agree with him

00:02:08.294 --> 00:02:09.595
all the time,
but it's very good.

00:02:09.595 --> 00:02:13.566
-It's very good.
-And then he goes --

00:02:13.566 --> 00:02:15.801
And then he misses his window,
and he's then awake.

00:02:15.801 --> 00:02:17.903
And he starts screaming.

00:02:17.903 --> 00:02:20.740
And for the --
almost the entire red-eye,

00:02:20.740 --> 00:02:22.809
he will not fall asleep.

00:02:22.809 --> 00:02:25.378
And, like, we have people
trying to give him advice.

00:02:25.378 --> 00:02:29.882
This woman, who I think was
at one point a model, came up.

00:02:29.882 --> 00:02:31.116
[ Laughter ]

00:02:31.116 --> 00:02:34.319
And she was, like,
"Maybe I should hold your baby."

00:02:34.319 --> 00:02:36.856
And she picked him up.

00:02:36.856 --> 00:02:38.458
And my son, like --

00:02:38.458 --> 00:02:40.726
You know, 'cause she looked like
a bunch of paper airplanes

00:02:40.726 --> 00:02:42.328
covered in marzipan.

00:02:42.328 --> 00:02:44.363
[ Laughter ]

00:02:44.363 --> 00:02:46.599
And my son freaked out.

00:02:46.599 --> 00:02:48.134
And so then
he's crying the entire --

00:02:48.134 --> 00:02:49.868
literally the entire flight.

00:02:49.868 --> 00:02:53.939
We land in Venice,
and this guy gets off the plane,

00:02:53.939 --> 00:02:57.276
and he's wearing a seersucker
suit and a Panama hat.

00:02:57.276 --> 00:02:58.777
I think it's like a mob boss.

00:02:58.777 --> 00:03:01.280
Like a proper
Italian Mafia boss.

00:03:01.280 --> 00:03:03.483
He is not happy about it.

00:03:03.483 --> 00:03:04.917
I then get to baggage claim.

00:03:04.917 --> 00:03:07.186
I realize,
it's not a Mafia boss.

00:03:07.186 --> 00:03:09.455
It's Brendan Fraser.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:09.455 --> 00:03:11.257
And he's so pissed.

00:03:11.257 --> 00:03:12.591
And then we go out that night,

00:03:12.591 --> 00:03:14.293
and I see Natasha Lyonne
is at the festival.

00:03:14.293 --> 00:03:15.327
-Yep.
-And she was like,

00:03:15.327 --> 00:03:16.362
[ Coarse voice ]
"How was your flight?"

00:03:16.362 --> 00:03:18.697
And I was like,
"It was all right.

00:03:18.697 --> 00:03:19.999
My kid cried a bunch."

00:03:19.999 --> 00:03:22.335
She's like, "That was your kid
on the plane?"

00:03:22.335 --> 00:03:24.604
[ Laughter ]

00:03:24.604 --> 00:03:26.606
She was like,
"That was like Lou Reed."

00:03:26.606 --> 00:03:28.507
And -- I don't know.
Whatever.

00:03:28.507 --> 00:03:32.945
Anyway, so, find out that
Brendan Fraser was talking about

00:03:32.945 --> 00:03:36.015
how much my son
was crying on the plane

00:03:36.015 --> 00:03:37.550
that he wouldn't fall asleep,

00:03:37.550 --> 00:03:39.018
he couldn't get
a good night's sleep.

00:03:39.018 --> 00:03:41.020
I was like, I felt terrible.
It's your worst nightmare

00:03:41.020 --> 00:03:42.388
that you're gonna be the people

00:03:42.388 --> 00:03:44.890
whose kid is screaming
on the red-eye.

00:03:44.890 --> 00:03:47.293
The next night,
I go to a premiere with my wife,

00:03:47.293 --> 00:03:49.228
and we go to see this movie
called "The Whale."

00:03:49.228 --> 00:03:51.664
-Starring Brendan Fraser.
-Right.

00:03:51.664 --> 00:03:53.499
[ Laughter ]

00:03:53.499 --> 00:03:55.635
And he plays
this, like, 600-pound man.

00:03:55.635 --> 00:03:59.205
And the movie,
he's amazing in the film.

00:03:59.205 --> 00:04:02.708
And he's one of my favorite
actors, from "Encino Man"

00:04:02.708 --> 00:04:05.911
to where he's a Jew
in "School Ties."

00:04:05.911 --> 00:04:08.748
-Yeah.
-So believable.

00:04:08.748 --> 00:04:11.183
[ Laughter ]

00:04:11.183 --> 00:04:13.419
To the documentary "The Mummy."
-Yeah.

00:04:13.419 --> 00:04:15.220
[ Laughter ]

00:04:15.220 --> 00:04:16.455
The follow-up documentary,
"The Mummy Returns."

00:04:16.455 --> 00:04:20.093
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.
-And then, finally,

00:04:20.093 --> 00:04:21.894
he's in this movie.
This is his big comeback.

00:04:21.894 --> 00:04:22.995
The movie finishes.

00:04:22.995 --> 00:04:25.497
He gets an eight-minute
standing ovation.

00:04:25.497 --> 00:04:27.633
People are -- he's crying.

00:04:27.633 --> 00:04:29.602
You can feel him being like,
"I'm back, baby.

00:04:29.602 --> 00:04:31.603
It's the Oscars.
Here we come."

00:04:31.603 --> 00:04:34.206
He then turns around,

00:04:34.206 --> 00:04:39.445
and me and my wife are standing
directly behind him.

00:04:39.445 --> 00:04:43.516
And he looks at us,
and then I pull up my baby.

00:04:43.516 --> 00:04:45.751
[ Laughter ]

00:04:45.751 --> 00:04:47.286
And he starts crying.

00:04:47.286 --> 00:04:49.354
And my wife
took a picture of him

00:04:49.354 --> 00:04:51.357
just at the moment
he looked at us.

00:04:51.357 --> 00:04:55.795
And if you can look closely,
you can see Brendan Fraser...

00:04:55.795 --> 00:04:57.797
[ Laughter ]

00:04:57.797 --> 00:05:00.566
...realizing that
we have ruined his night.

00:05:00.566 --> 00:05:02.601
[ Laughter ]

00:05:02.601 --> 00:05:05.237
-"The one person I said
don't give a ticket to

00:05:05.237 --> 00:05:07.006
was Kroll's baby."
-I know!

00:05:07.006 --> 00:05:08.574
What are you gonna do?
I mean...

00:05:08.574 --> 00:05:10.442
-Congratulations on the special.
It's fantastic.

00:05:10.442 --> 00:05:11.544
It's always a pleasure
to see you.

00:05:11.544 --> 00:05:13.279
Nick Kroll!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:13.279 --> 00:05:14.447
"Little Big Boy"
is streaming on Netflix.

00:05:14.447 --> 00:05:15.714
And "Don't Worry Darling"
is in theater's now.

00:05:15.714 --> 00:05:17.216
We'll be right back
with Steve-O.

